$ whycant -u root write /var/log/audit.trail

✗ root (uid 0) cannot write /var/log/audit.trail

  /                      drwxr-xr-x      root:root  ✓ traverse
  /var                   drwxr-xr-x      root:root  ✓ traverse
  /var/log               drwxr-xr-x      root:root  ✓ traverse
  /var/log/audit.trail   -rw-r--r-- [a]  root:root  ✗ write   ← blocked here

Why
  /var/log/audit.trail has the append-only attribute: it can only be opened for appending,
  so normal writes fail, even for root. Appending still works; to check that:
  whycant append /var/log/audit.trail

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Remove the attribute (someone set this on purpose; find out why first):
       sudo chattr -a /var/log/audit.trail
